{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## OVERNIGHT AUTONOMOUS MODE -- primary: keep main green; secondary: orphan bugs\n\nOperator set standing instructions: running overnight, do not prompt for input, do not block. Other\nsessions executing epics have been told I own orphan bugs and main-green. Acting accordingly -- no\nmore AskUserQuestion; I make the call, state the assumption, and keep going.\n\n### MAIN-GREEN STATE (the primary job)\n\nThree known main-red items, one now fixed:\n\n1. 9a17 -- FIXED. Change 2600 merged as 668523feffde (operator submitted it past the scanner block).\n   All five ACs verified against the MERGED tree, not the agent's report: timeout= at\n   _toolchain.py:103 with the named error at :111; portable e2e-deps at Makefile:470; cache keyed on\n   node-version + hashFiles(package-lock.json) at _build-and-test.yml:474 with npm ci at Makefile:493;\n   fcntl.LOCK_EX at :86. Close running.\n\n2. scanner-integration -- ANOTHER SESSION OWNS IT. Stood down, handed over findings on 90c7. Proven\n   to fail on MAIN itself (dispatched run 33839813271), so it is not a property of changes trying to\n   land. Two distinct faults confirmed: change 2600 hit a genuine missing-file error on its older\n   base, while main and change 2607 both HAVE the file and fail anyway.\n\n3. sweep (windows) -- NEW FINDING, MINE, agent dispatched. It has failed on EVERY recent scheduled\n   branch-head run: 01:07, 18:48, 12:52, 06:55. Every sibling sweep job passes in those same runs\n   (py3.14, py3.14t, py3.15, macos full suite, declared lower-bound, external doc links). Nobody was\n   tracking it. Since branch health only refreshes ~6-hourly and main is deliberately excluded from\n   push-triggered runs, a defect here can sit unseen for hours.\n\nMONITOR ARMED (persistent) reporting two things and otherwise silent: any CI run that FAILS, and\nevery branch-head result on main regardless of outcome. Primed against already-completed runs so only\nnew results surface. NOTE MY OWN BUG WORTH REMEMBERING: my first monitor read os.environ['SEEN'] but\nI only set a shell variable and never exported it, so it would have silently emitted nothing --\nan armed watch that is actually blind. Caught and rewritten before relying on it.\n\nALSO LEARNED: test.yml's concurrency group CANCELS in-progress runs on the same ref, so my second\nmanual dispatch killed the first. One branch-head dispatch at a time.\n\n### NEW TICKETS THIS STRETCH\n\n337e-b558-17a2-49bd / diseased-witless-bluebird (p2): browser_runner NEVER EXECUTES in CI -- nothing\nruns 'npx playwright install chromium', so the tier self-skips on 'Chromium unavailable' and the\ngreen is partly vacuous. Filed with the fork stated rather than assumed: either run the tier, or make\nthe skip LOUD and INTENTIONAL. Option (b) is explicitly not treated as the lesser choice -- the tier\nmay be local-only by design; what is unacceptable is a silent skip that looks like coverage.\n\nThis is the THIRD defect today of one shape: ABSENCE OF EXECUTION REPORTED AS SUCCESS. 9a17 (a\nworker kill reported as a crash, hiding a timeout), 90c7 (a job that never ran, yet its change got\nVerified +1), and now this. Worth watching for as a class, not three incidents.\n\nDUPLICATE I CREATED AND CLEANED UP: I filed c5ca for the toolchain fast-path race 14 seconds after\nthe agent had already filed 477b for the same thing, because I did not search first. Closed c5ca as\nclass=duplicate, carried its two unique ACs onto 477b. The close gate correctly refused until I added\na 'duplicates' LINK rather than 'relates_to' -- its reasoning is good and worth knowing: without the\nlink there is nothing to verify, because the work lives on the replacement, so completion\nverification would be asking the duplicate to prove work it never owned.\n\n### BOARD: 9 orphan bugs\nopen: 6f66 (p3 anthropic order-dependence), a1f1 (p2 mechanism ratchet), 90c7 (p0, other session),\n337e (p2 chromium), 477b (p2 toolchain race)\nin_progress: 3276 (p1), 740d (p2, change 2601), 9ea3 (p1), ae97 (p1, change 2608), c379 (p2, change\n2607), 9a17 (p0, closing)\n\nChanges awaiting votes: 2594, 2601, 2607, 2608, 2609. All were blocked behind 9a17 and/or the scanner\njob; 9a17 is now cleared, so their next CI runs are the real test."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788500768530574001,"uuid":"0c6465fd-6ea5-42c1-b69f-4723c61d3cf1"}